# THE BOOK TEXT NEVER ENTERS AN IMAGE.
#
# `data/` holds the corpus, the gazetteer and the alias seeds; `sessions/` holds
# harvested D&D Beyond pages. Both are copyrighted, both are kept out of git for
# that reason, and an image is a thing that gets pushed to a registry and pulled
# by whoever can reach it -- so the same rule has to be written down twice. A
# bare `COPY . .` without this file bakes 1.6 million characters of two
# published books into a layer.
#
# The graph is populated over bolt by `backend.scripts.push_graph`, so the
# running container needs none of it.
data/
sessions/

.env
.env.local
.venv/
venv/

.git/
.github/
web/
node_modules/
evals/
docs/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
tests/
